---
/*
  VocabActions — the Save / Merge… / Delete cluster on a Library row.

  WRITTEN FOUR TIMES BEFORE THIS (plan 38 · §4.3), once per vocabulary, and that
  is why §1.2's fix waited for §4.3: replacing the merge control in four places
  means building the replacement four times, which is what plans 16 and 19 have
  already half-done once between them.

  ⚠ THE MERGE CONTROL WAS A `<select>` AND IS NOW A BUTTON, AND THAT IS A
  BEHAVIOUR FIX RATHER THAN A TIDY-UP. The old one hung the merge on the
  select's `change` event: tab to "Merge into…" and press ↓ and the browser
  changes the value and fires `change`, so a confirm opened proposing to merge
  the row you were standing on into the first alphabetical entity. Merge
  reassigns every link and HARD-DELETES the loser — the dialog's own words are
  "This can't be undone." The decline path reset the value so it recovered, but
  a `<select>` is a value control and this is an action. A button cannot be
  triggered by an arrow key.

  ⚠ AND IT TAKES 11,309 `<option>` ELEMENTS OUT OF THE PAGE. Every row rendered
  every OTHER row as an option — O(n²), and 86% of this page's DOM by plan 19's
  count. The picker reads one JSON payload per vocabulary instead, so the cost
  is linear and the same list serves every row.

  The rejected alternative is "just add a confirm", which is what it already had:
  the confirm was never the missing piece, the arrow key was.
*/
interface Props {
  /** Which vocabulary — the key the page's action map is dialled by. */
  entity: 'subject' | 'feeling' | 'author' | 'work';
  /** This row's id, so the picker can exclude it from its own target list. */
  id: string;
  /** This row's name, so the confirm can say what is being merged AWAY. */
  name: string;
}
const { entity, id, name } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
  <button class="lib-save btn btn-primary btn-xs normal-case">Save</button>
  {
    /* `data-lib-merge` rather than the old `.lib-merge` class, deliberately: the
      class named a `<select>` that no longer exists, and a stale selector that
      still matches something is worse than one that matches nothing. */
  }
  <button
    type="button"
    data-lib-merge
    data-entity={entity}
    data-id={id}
    data-name={name}
    class="btn btn-ghost btn-xs normal-case">Merge…</button
  >
  <button class="lib-delete btn btn-ghost btn-xs text-error normal-case">Delete</button>
</div>
